CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ deleted: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^\[main\.pointer_dereference\.\d+\] .*: FAILURE$
--
The destructor of a delete-expression was called unconditionally, so for a
null pointer to a class with a virtual destructor its vtable pointer was
read through the null pointer.
